  "summary": {
    "en": [
      "Branka M. Malinar Branka M. Malinar – Biography Branka Malinar was born in Popovec, Croatia in 1941. At the age of four, the family fled the Communist Revolution in Croatia and escaped to Austria to a DP (refugee) camp. After living in the camp for two years, they moved to Munich, Germany. The final leg of their migration took them across the Atlantic Ocean traveling on the S.S. General Muir arrived on Ellis Island on May 17th, 1951. The family that sponsored them through Catholic charities helped them to settle in Cleveland, Ohio. Family Life and..."
    ]
